Package: gatekeepR
Title: Reviewable Marker Gating and Phenotyping for Multiplexed Imaging
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("R.", "Heller",
           email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: Turns per-cell marker measurements from multiplexed tissue
    images into reviewed cell types and state calls. Declares a marker
    panel and an ordered phenotype hierarchy as data, decides per image
    whether each marker can be called at all, and estimates thresholds
    with documented methods (manual, density valley, density tail,
    two-component Gaussian mixture, population density crossing on an
    embedding and parent-specific crossing). A single classifier is
    shared by batch code and the review application. Reviewer decisions
    are kept in append-only ledgers, and a review is locked into a
    content-addressed export whose labels, decisions and deletion
    histories can be replayed and verified.
